      "content": "I get the \"proactive\" angle, but looking at the actual data from the penetration testers, there aren't really any \"minor gaps\" to plug. The report is basically a straight line of success. \n\nIf we tell them there are gaps just to sell the package and they find out later there weren't any issues, won't that damage our credibility? Is there a way to make the upgrade feel necessary based on the actual findings, even if the findings themselves are good?",
